From 165d5d7b3abc1c331365227a4028bc3ee590f055 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 06:18:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add Qt4 build support behind QT_VERSION guards

Converseen's Qt5-only surface is small enough to emulate, so the tree can
target Qt4, Qt5 and Qt6 from one source. Every Qt4 path sits behind a
QT_VERSION guard, leaving Qt5/Qt6 behavior unchanged.

New src/qt4compat.h provides, for Qt4 only:
  - a QStandardPaths shim over QDesktopServices::storageLocation()/XDG that
    resolves to the same paths Qt5 uses, so existing settings are still found
  - QCommandLineOption/QCommandLineParser supporting aliases, "-o value",
    "--opt=value", valueless flags, --help and --version. Unknown options are
    skipped rather than fatal, so the macOS Finder's -psn_x_y argument does
    not stop the bundle from launching
  - Q_OS_MACOS/Q_OS_OSX aliases for Qt4's Q_OS_MAC

Guarded at the call sites:
  - QStorageInfo::rootPath() falls back to "/" (only AppImage differs)
  - QScreen/QGuiApplication device pixel ratio falls back to 1.0
  - AA_EnableHighDpiScaling, AA_UseHighDpiPixmaps, setDesktopFileName
  - QtConcurrent/QFutureWatcher includes; the directory scan runs inline
  - QComboBox::currentTextChanged() -> currentIndexChanged()
  - QHeaderView::setSectionResizeMode() -> setResizeMode()

The .ui files drop 3 toolTipDuration properties (all -1, the default) and 2
stepType properties, which Qt4's uic cannot emit. Adaptive stepping is
restored from code under a Qt 5.12 guard, so Qt5/Qt6 lose nothing.
showGroupSeparator is left alone: it is stdset="0", so uic emits setProperty()
and Qt4 treats it as a no-op.

Build with -DUSE_QT4=ON, or plain qmake, which detects QT_MAJOR_VERSION.
Qt4 builds use C++11, since Qt4 headers still use the register keyword.

